Initial Import:
First, save the excel spreadsheet as a CSV (Comma Deliniated), not CSV UTF-8, important distinction for proper importing formatting. Create a new schema, then right click the table on the side bar and press the implementation wizard and select the CSV. 

Inside Import Wizard:
This is extremely important, during the import you will arrive at a configure import settings screen, make sure to press the wrench and change the field separator to comma. After this you're free to complete the import process.

During Import: (Asked Gemini AI how to speed up import)
The actual import through the wizard would take a few hours, however I found a method that speeds this up. First, give it a moment to import a few entries to ensure the table is properly formatted, then you can cancel it. 
Once canceled, you can use this bulk import query to instantly import everything into it's proper rows and columns. 

LOAD DATA LOCAL INFILE '(insert csv filepath)'
INTO TABLE (insert name of created table)
FIELDS TERMINATED BY ',' 
ENCLOSED BY '"'
LINES TERMINATED BY '\r\n'
IGNORE 1 ROWS;

The reason running the wizard first is mandatory is so it handles the table creation, making and assigning the rows, columns, and attributes for you. It's just a faster method than doing it manually.
